{
  "v": 2,
  "order": 510,
  "label": "Decision Matrix",
  "group": "Worked examples",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "noteIntro",
      "type": "NoteNode",
      "x": -60,
      "y": 758,
      "init": {
        "label": "Decision Matrix",
        "body": "# Weighted scoring, ranked\nA **Decision Matrix** scores a table of options against weighted criteria and ranks them.\n\n**Flow:** a Frame of scores (rows are options, number columns are criteria) → **Decision Matrix** → `Option · Score · Rank`, best first. The Screen column comes from a **Note**: its frontmatter emits a keyed table, joined in by laptop name, and its text records the reasoning. A **Report** at the end pulls the results into a live memo.\n\nA small **Weights** table wires in one row per criterion: a **weight** (default 1; negative = lower is better, like Price) and an optional **Norm** override. Score = **Σ(value × weight) / Σ|weight|**. Tweak a weight and watch the ranking move.",
        "color": "violet",
        "width": 400,
        "height": 300
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "scores",
      "type": "FrameInputNode",
      "x": 426,
      "y": 796,
      "init": {
        "label": "Score table",
        "frameText": "[{\"name\":\"Laptop\",\"type\":\"string\",\"values\":[\"ProBook\",\"UltraSlim\",\"PowerLifter\",\"Budget\"]},{\"name\":\"Performance\",\"type\":\"number\",\"values\":[9,6,10,4]},{\"name\":\"Battery\",\"type\":\"number\",\"values\":[6,9,5,7]},{\"name\":\"Price\",\"type\":\"number\",\"values\":[1800,1400,2200,700]}]"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "noteScreen",
      "type": "NoteNode",
      "x": 738,
      "y": 803,
      "init": {
        "label": "Screen scores",
        "body": "---\nscreen:\n  - {Laptop: ProBook, Screen: 8}\n  - {Laptop: UltraSlim, Screen: 9}\n  - {Laptop: PowerLifter, Screen: 7}\n  - {Laptop: Budget, Screen: 5}\n---\n### Screen scores\nProBook 8: 4K panel with an anti-glare coating. UltraSlim 9: brightest of the four. PowerLifter 7: sharp but reflective. Budget 5: a review flagged weak brightness.\n\nThe frontmatter rows emit a keyed table directly, one **frame** output, so each score stays attached to its laptop however the main table is sorted.",
        "color": "amber",
        "width": 400,
        "height": 250
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "join",
      "type": "JoinNode",
      "x": 1398,
      "y": 758,
      "init": {
        "label": "Join on Laptop",
        "how": "left"
      },
      "stringLiterals": {
        "leftKey": "Laptop",
        "rightKey": "Laptop"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dm",
      "type": "DecisionMatrixNode",
      "x": 2047,
      "y": 364,
      "init": {
        "label": "Decision Matrix",
        "normalize": "max",
        "detail": "breakdown"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "weights",
      "type": "FrameInputNode",
      "x": 1765,
      "y": 415,
      "init": {
        "label": "Weights",
        "frameText": "[{\"name\":\"Criterion\",\"type\":\"string\",\"values\":[\"Performance\",\"Battery\",\"Screen\",\"Price\"]},{\"name\":\"Weight\",\"type\":\"number\",\"values\":[3,2,1,-2]},{\"name\":\"Norm\",\"type\":\"string\",\"values\":[\"\",\"\",\"\",\"Rank\"]}]"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "noteDM",
      "type": "NoteNode",
      "x": 1982,
      "y": 729,
      "init": {
        "label": "Mixed scales, one range",
        "body": "Price is in **dollars**; the rest are out of **10**. Scored raw, the dollar column would swamp everything, so each column is first squeezed onto the same footing; then only the **weights** decide influence.\n\n**÷Max** divides a column by its biggest value, so each tops out at 1. **Rank** keeps only the order: $2,200 counts as “most expensive”, not as 2,200 of anything. Price uses Rank; the rest follow the ÷Max default.\n\n**Breakdown** is on: each criterion column is its **signed contribution**, and the contributions sum to the Score. Price shows negative, the penalty it is.",
        "color": "green",
        "width": 370,
        "height": 280
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "select",
      "type": "ColumnsNode",
      "x": 2482,
      "y": 813,
      "init": {
        "label": "Keep Laptop · Score"
      },
      "stringLiterals": {
        "columns": "Laptop,Score"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "chart",
      "type": "ChartNode",
      "x": 2807,
      "y": 805,
      "init": {
        "label": "Podium",
        "op": "bar"
      },
      "stringLiterals": {
        "options": "title=Weighted score;xlabel=Score"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "noteChart",
      "type": "NoteNode",
      "x": 2430,
      "y": 427,
      "init": {
        "label": "The podium is a chart",
        "body": "The ranking is already the table. For the podium, **Select Columns** keeps `Laptop · Score`, and a two-column frame into **Chart** draws labeled bars: the first column names them, the second sets the lengths.",
        "color": "vermilion",
        "width": 320,
        "height": 160
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "winner",
      "type": "ListIndexNode",
      "x": 2478,
      "y": 232,
      "init": {
        "label": "Winner"
      },
      "literals": {
        "index": 1,
        "column": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "report",
      "type": "ReportNode",
      "x": 2839,
      "y": 330,
      "init": {
        "label": "Decision memo",
        "body": "# Laptop pick\n\nWith the weights on the canvas, the matrix picks `=winner!`.\n\n`=podium`\n\nBehind the bars, each criterion column is a signed contribution; the contributions sum to the Score, and Price counts against:\n\n`=ranking`\n\nEvery figure here is wired. Change a weight or a score upstream and the memo follows."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "noteSens",
      "type": "NoteNode",
      "x": 1857,
      "y": 1423,
      "init": {
        "label": "Sensitivity",
        "body": "# Stress-test the weights\nThe winner depends on the weights picked above. **Sensitivity** re-scores the same options under several weight **scenarios**, one per weight column of the Scenarios frame, and returns a **Cube**: per scenario the **Winner**, the **Margin** (top score minus runner-up), and the full **Ranking** nested in the cell. Drill in.\n\nThe winner flips: **UltraSlim** under Balanced, **PowerLifter** when performance dominates. Under Budget the Winner cell reads **UltraSlim = Budget**, a dead tie at Margin 0. That pick is fragile; the first two hold.",
        "color": "blue",
        "width": 380,
        "height": 280
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "scenarios",
      "type": "FrameInputNode",
      "x": 1763,
      "y": 1128,
      "init": {
        "label": "Weight scenarios",
        "frameText": "[{\"name\":\"Criterion\",\"type\":\"string\",\"values\":[\"Performance\",\"Battery\",\"Screen\",\"Price\"]},{\"name\":\"Balanced\",\"type\":\"number\",\"values\":[3,2,1,-2]},{\"name\":\"Performance-first\",\"type\":\"number\",\"values\":[5,1,1,-1]},{\"name\":\"Budget\",\"type\":\"number\",\"values\":[1,1,1,-5]}]"
      }
    },
